[ ] Project recurring occurrences into the action surfaces =occurrence-surface $Client-surface follow-on to VTODO sync: the action list becomes a windowed union of materialized actions + projected occurrences (render(master+deviations, window)). Occurrences have no .actions line. Seam: operations uniform, text-editing not. See README 'Client-surface projection (2026-07-24)'.$ !2 #019f962c-ba5a-7732-ad24-df6fceadea53
    >[ ] Surface occurrences in nvim as virtual lines and code-actions $Keep the buffer honest: occurrences render as virtual lines/extmarks, never editable buffer text with nowhere to save back. Expose complete/reschedule/skip as LSP code-actions that invoke the occurrence-ops write path. org-agenda two-surface model: raw-file editing unchanged for materialized actions.$ !3 <occurrence-ops #019f962d-1f15-7c23-82d5-e1c8f2a652e0
    >[x] Seal the projection to sync leak $Sync reconciles owned artifacts only; a projected occurrence has no standalone resource to reconcile and no line for apply_sync to locate. sync_calendar now loads a window-0 model (Projection::without_occurrences / ctx.load_model_materialized) so occurrences are structurally absent from plan_sync, not filtered by a fragile flag. Regression-locked in workspace_store.rs. Relates to the two-assembly-sites debt in =occurrence-view.$ #019f9bdf-bad8-7940-a77e-98be6bf8b04e
[ ] Build the templated recurrence stamping lane =stamping-lane ~ $Stateful (multi-step, template:) recurring plans, the second lane. A templated plan is cron for actions: on its schedule an idempotent generator stamps the template into .actions as a real, dead-on-arrival subtree. GRAFT model: synthesize the occurrence root from the master VTODO (SUMMARY->title, CATEGORIES->contexts, PRIORITY->priority, id = occurrence UUIDv5 = hash(plan UID, slot)) and graft the template step-forest beneath it via the dead-since-expand parent_override in instantiate_template. No parentless-children invariant to relax. See README design notes 2026-07-26 cont.$ !2 +caldav #019fa019-079f-7681-bb22-d64ab1a9f78c
    >[ ] Stamp templated plans on the write path $The one net-new function: for each templated plan, for each due, non-EXDATE-d slot with no existing action (id = hash(plan UID, slot)), stamp the template. Idempotency = deterministic root id + the existing materialized-wins-by-id union (re-stamping an existing slot is a no-op); the workspace is the watermark. Skip = EXDATE on the master (shared with atomic recurrence). Lives on the write path (sync calendar / a tick verb), never on the pure From<Workspace> load. Reuses instantiate_template with the occurrence UUIDv5 as the root id and no parent override. Deferred knob: cap catch-up stamps after a long gap so it cannot flood.$ !2 +caldav #019fa019-3db7-7a13-8ae1-88937dd3ccdf
    >[ ] Round-trip stamped-root completion to the master deviation $Templated completion is calendar-managed: completing the stamped ROOT writes a completed RECURRENCE-ID override on the master via write_occurrence_deviation (the atomic-lane path), keyed by the root id = occurrence key. The rich interior stays local in .actions; only the rollup bit reaches the calendar. Live linkage = (plan_id, slot) stamped into PlansSyncStore at stamp time, consumed/cleared when the deviation lands (needed because the slot key is unrecoverable from the hash id or the mutable scheduled_at). Stamped instances must NOT also flatten to standalone VTODOs (avoids foreign double-vision against the master RRULE) — exclude them at the loader/sync boundary like the window-0 loader already does for projected occurrences.$ !2 +caldav #019fa019-3dc6-7060-b744-34a7279ee420
    >[ ] Snapshot plan-lineage onto the archived instance at completion $A completion is an immutable fact and must be self-contained. At crystallization (completion/archival) snapshot the SEMANTIC edge onto the archived instance: realizes plan-M at temporal position T, plus a human label so it survives the plan being deleted. Do NOT reverse-derive from the current RRULE (may be edited/deleted since) — the invoice-snapshots-price-at-sale principle. Layer-sensitive: while live, lineage is derived from the current rule (sync-store cache stands); the snapshot happens only at the phase transition. Snapshot the semantic edge, never the occurrence-id hash.$ !3 +caldav #019fa019-3dd0-7993-bcae-c0abfbf8f60d
[ ] Add a delete verb, distinct from close/cancel $Consequence of the fact-model: there is no immutability invariant (unenforceable across hand-editable plaintext + foreign CalDAV clients + eventually-consistent sync, so declaring it would be a lie). close/cancel are STATE TRANSITIONS (the fact persists, status changes); delete is RETRACTION FROM HISTORY (erase the thing). The user declares intent via the verb; the system does not infer human-vs-machine provenance. Safe because graphd degrades gracefully over a tolerant world (dangling refs / missing nodes / partial reads) — a deleted fact is a hole a projection absorbs. History-preserving stays the default by convention; delete is the deliberate, higher-friction exception. NOTE: likely a general workspace/action-lifecycle verb, not caldav-specific — may belong in a core charter; seeded here because the fact-model that motivates it is documented in this README.$ !3 +caldav #019fa019-5d05-7ee0-a09a-b4e20c2a304a
